{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793473481,"nonce":"zoyuet7trBfuHtuMuca8RFva3S8=","title":"Cargo.lock is not tracked, so a build from a committed tree resolves dependencies afresh","message":".gitignore excludes Cargo.lock, so `git archive` of a commit, a fresh clone or a git dependency pinned by rev resolves every dependency version again (and the wasmtime git rev from the manifest) instead of the lockfile the commit was tested with. The repository ships executables (zylua, zypy, zynml), for which Cargo recommends committing the lockfile. Reported by the dynASB embedding session (their git-bug 5b7d11d); ef59064 was a build that broke for the same reason.","files":null}]}